632	  <p>Full pass across path handling, SQL construction, deserialization, and command execution in this session's diff — zero findings crossed the 8/10 confidence bar. <code>lumen-store</code> uses parameterized <code>rusqlite</code> queries consistently, no diff introduces string-built SQL, and every untrusted JSONL field is extracted through typed, defaulting accessors with no <code>unsafe</code> anywhere in the workspace (enforced by <code>#![forbid(unsafe_code)]</code>). One latent note, not a live finding: <code>AgyAdapter::resolve_transcript_path</code> has no traversal guard on its <code>conversation_id</code> argument, but nothing in this diff calls it with untrusted input yet — worth guarding when it's wired up, not urgent now.</p>
633	</section>
